# Rust/Tauri native layer

- Native code owns CS2 process management, NetCon, capture, sidecar lifecycle and secure OS integration.
- Never use DLL injection or process-memory APIs for CS2.
- Never construct shell commands from user-controlled strings.
- Prefer typed process arguments.
- Console commands must pass through an allowlist/typed command builder.
- Add timeouts to network and child-process operations.
- Capture failures must be recoverable.
- Keep Tauri commands narrow and typed.
- Do not move tactical/business rules into Rust.
